      {
        "position": 7,
        "title": "Good flea comb, but only for short-haired pets",
        "text": "This is a great quality flea comb with sturdy bristles. I like that the bristles are well rounded to avoid scratching, and the distance between them is perfect for its intended use.However, I do think the bristles should be a bit longer. I’m using it to brush my cats, who are just standard American shorthairs, and the bristles do reach their skin. On a longer-haired cat, though, I think you would definitely have trouble brushing deeply enough to actually catch any fleas closer to the skin.The handle is also a bit bulky and made of hard plastic, but the grooves make it easy to hold. There is no coating on the handle, so there’s nothing to chip off over time, which means it will probably last a long time. Unfortunately, that also means the handle is pretty uncomfortable. Overall, this is a good comb, but the handle may make prolonged use uncomfortable, and I don’t recommend it for long-haired pets.",
